==English==
{{wikipedia|Alternative words for British}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|Briton or Englishman}} {{l|en|Pom}}

===Etymology===
A [[clipping]] of {{m|en|pomegranate}}. In reference to the British, first attested in Australia in 1912<ref>'''1998''', Roger Robinson, Nelson Wattie, ''The Oxford Companion to New Zealand Literature'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=L8cUAQAAIAAJ&pg=PA445 page 445].</ref><ref>http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/magazine-22378819</ref> as [[rhyming slang]] for {{m|en|immigrant}} with additional reference to the likelihood of [[sunburn]] turning their skin pomegranate red. As a cocktail, originally American.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɒm/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɑm/|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɔm/|a=AU}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-pom.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒm|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Australia|NZ|South Africa|mildly|_|pejorative|_|slang}} An [[Englishman]]; a [[Briton]]; a [[person]] of [[British]] [[descent]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1987|author=Linda Christmas|title=The Ribbon and the Ragged Square: An Australian Journey|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=1Bfo6Rd90NEC&q=%22pom%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&dq=%22pom%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=mN7iT4u-PKXimAX_xt3VAw&redir_esc=y|page=27
|passage=I could see more than mere humour in car stickers that read ‘Grow your own Dope: Plant a '''Pom'''’ ... ‘Keep Australia Beautiful: Shoot a '''Pom'''’.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1989|author=Tony Wheeler|title=Australia: A Travel Survival Kit|publisher=Lonely Planet|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=nHEUAQAAMAAJ&q=%22pom%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&dq=%22pom%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=mN7iT4u-PKXimAX_xt3VAw&redir_esc=y|page=10
|passage=The prize for being Australia′s original '''pom''' goes to the enterprising pirate William Dampier, who made the first investigations ashore about 40 years after Tasman and nearly 100 years before Cook.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Lawrence Booth|title=Cricket, Lovely Cricket?|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=zO3VL4ybLQwC&pg=PA214&dq=%22pom%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=mN7iT4u-PKXimAX_xt3VAw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22pom%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=214
|passage=At one stage a group called British People Against Racial Discrimination complained to the Advertising Standards Board in Australia about an advert for Tooheys beer that claimed it was ‘cold enough to scare a '''Pom'''’.}}
# {{lb|en|cocktail}} A [[cocktail]] [[contain]]ing [[pomegranate]] [[juice]] and [[vodka]].

====Usage notes====
Whether ''pom'', {{m|en|pommy}}, etc. is sometimes considered an ethnic or racial slur within the [[Commonwealth]], largely by British expatriates; however the advertising boards of both Australia and New Zealand reject this.

